# End-to-end order
#
# Shows:   an end-to-end macro — both sides of an order in one file and one
#          run: a `run` block that sends and an `on order` block that answers,
#          each giving its own verdict
# Needs:   the loopback sessions; run with LOOP-CLI as the client session
#          and LOOP-MKT as the market session
# Watch:   Sent Orders and Received Orders side by side; End-to-end Macro
#          Runs (Macro menu): the order twice under one run, once a side
# Outcome: the order is accepted, half filled, replaced up to 300 and
#          cancelled with 50 done; the client side passes on what it heard,
#          the market side on what it was asked

run
    new symbol: 'IBM', side: buy, qty: 100, type: limit, price: 10
    expect ack within 2s
    expect fill within 5s
    replace qty: 300
    expect replaced within 2s else fail 'the replace was not answered'
    cancel
    expect canceled within 2s
    if order.cum_qty != 50
        fail 'done ${order.cum_qty}, not the 50 that were filled'
    pass '${order.cl_ord_id} cancelled with ${order.cum_qty} done'

# The same run's other half: the order arrives here, under the ClOrdID the
# block above gave it. An end-to-end run is offered what arrives before any
# Market or Client run is, so a desk that happens to be armed does not
# answer the test's orders.
on order where symbol == 'IBM'
    when replace
        if order.pending_qty < order.cum_qty
            reject text: 'below what is done'
        else
            accept
    when cancel
        let left = order.leaves_qty             # as it stands before the cancel is accepted
        accept
        pass 'asked to cancel ${order.cl_ord_id} with ${left} left'

    after 200ms
    accept
    after 1s
    fill qty: order.order_qty / 2, price: order.price
